    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32-a2">

                <pb facs="0147" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg47"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 277.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seymour to
                            Viceroy Chang.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-10T18:00:00+08:05"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi>,
                            10, 1883—6 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In drawing your excellency’s attention to
                    the lamentable occurrences which have this day resulted in such a destruction of
                    the property of the citizens of various western nations on Shameen, I feel it to
                    be my duty to represent that this destruction is due to the total want of
                    sufficient protection to the foreign settlement, and to the tardy action of the
                    Chinese authorities in sending a military force for our defense.</p>
                <p>I must most urgently impress upon your excellency the necessity of adopting
                    stringent measures to repress incendiaries and robbers.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>CHARLES SEYMOUR.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
